{"id":"email.headerregistry/DateHeader","module":"email.headerregistry","qualname":"DateHeader","name":"DateHeader","kind":"class","parent":null,"signatures":[],"doc":"Header whose value consists of a single timestamp.\n\nProvides an additional attribute, datetime, which is either an aware\ndatetime using a timezone, or a naive datetime if the timezone\nin the input string is -0000.  Also accepts a datetime as input.\nThe 'value' attribute is the normalized form of the timestamp,\nwhich means it is the output of format_datetime on the datetime.","docsUrl":"https://docs.python.org/3.15/library/email.headerregistry.html#email.headerregistry.DateHeader","added":null,"changed":[],"deprecated":null,"availability":[],"source":{"path":"Lib/email/headerregistry.py","line":274},"implDetail":false,"isAsync":false},
{"id":"email.headerregistry/DateHeader.datetime","module":"email.headerregistry","qualname":"DateHeader.datetime","name":"datetime","kind":"attribute","parent":"email.headerregistry/DateHeader","signatures":[],"doc":"If the header value can be recognized as a valid date of one form or another, this attribute will contain a datetime instance representing that date. If the timezone of the input date is specified as -0000 (indicating it is in UTC but contains no information about the source timezone), then datetime will be a naive datetime. If a specific timezone offset is found (including +0000), then datetime will contain an aware datetime that uses datetime.timezone to record the timezone offset.","docsUrl":"https://docs.python.org/3.15/library/email.headerregistry.html#email.headerregistry.DateHeader.datetime","added":null,"changed":[],"deprecated":null,"availability":[],"source":{"path":"Lib/email/headerregistry.py","line":315},"implDetail":false,"isAsync":false},
